I replaced the linear scan with a one-time-built direct lookup table indexed by message number, filling it in reverse so duplicates still return the first occurrence. Repeated lookups become a single array access instead of scanning the profile array.

```cpp
const Profile::MESG* Profile::GetMesg(const FIT_UINT16 num)
{
    static const Profile::MESG* lookup[65536] = {};
    static bool initialized = false;

    if (!initialized)
    {
        for (int i = MESGS - 1; i >= 0; --i)
        {
            lookup[mesgs[i].num] = &mesgs[i];
        }
        initialized = true;
    }

    return lookup[num];
}
```